===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|it|lingua franca}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlɪŋ.ɡwə ˈfɹæŋ.kə/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Persent101-lingua franca.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|+|lingue franche|linguae francae|linguas franca|pl4qual=rare|nolinkhead=1}} {{q|see usage notes}}

# A [[common]] [[language]] used by [[people]] of [[diverse]] [[background]]s to [[communicate]] with one another, often a [[basic]] [[form]] of [[speech]] with [[simplified]] [[grammar]], particularly, one that is not the [[first language]] of any of its [[speaker]]s.
#: {{syn|en|koine|link language|trade language|vehicular language}}
#: {{cot|en|vernacular}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|developer=w:BioWare|title={{w|Mass Effect: Andromeda}}|genre=[[science fiction|Science Fiction]]|location=Redwood City|publisher=Electronic Arts|year=2017|system=PC|scene=Angara: Languages Codex entry|oclc=1261299044|text=The language used by most angara across the Heleus Cluster is Shelesh, a '''lingua franca''' that was commonly used in the early days of angaran spaceflight before fading into obscurity. New connections between angaran settlements, and constant evolution of languages since their separation, means it has now seen a revival.}}

====Usage notes====
* The most common plural form in English is {{m|en|lingua francas}}; however, the plural forms {{m|en|lingue franche}} (following the Italian) and {{m|en|linguae francae}} (in the style of Latin) are both fairly common as well. Also attested, but quite rare, is the form {{m|en|linguas franca}} (treating {{m|en||lingua}} alone as the noun and taking {{m|en||franca}} as an adjective; compare {{m|en|attorney general|attorneys general}}, {{m|en|forest primeval|forests primeval}}).

